Subject: [PATCH 48/55] Drone tracks: Shift while recording a drone row's
 pitch: Select's fine steps, the knob deletes the lane cleanly

Turning a drone row's pitch while recording went through AutoParam's Shift branch, which
deletes the automation: Shift + Select (0.1 Hz steps otherwise) and Shift + the upper gold
knob deleted the whole Hz lane, and the lane's last value stayed on as the expression's
current value. noteOn() kept reading it and the song saved it as a constant, so the row
played detuned for good, with no lane and nothing in its frequency menu to show why.

Now, while recording:
- Shift + Select records its 0.1 Hz (or 1 cent) steps into the lane like any other turn.
  AutoParam::setCurrentValueInResponseToUserInput() takes shiftDeletesAutomation for that;
  its default keeps every other caller as it was.
- Shift + the upper gold knob deletes the lane, as Shift and a gold knob delete any
  automation while recording, and sets the value back to 0: the row returns to its tone's
  own pitch at once and is saved without an offset. The popup says the automation was
  deleted.

Test: mastertune tests/song/drone_edit_emu.py (run.sh DRONE=1).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Eb214cM1zi1k5Gpcn9RLKh
